---
import ContractStory from "../components/landing/ContractStory";
import Ecosystem from "../components/landing/Ecosystem.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> CONTRACT TESTING FOR AGENTIC APPS</div>
    <h1>Agents change.<br /><em>Keep your UI in sync.</em></h1>
    <p>Breaking tool contracts. Caught before deploy.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="/docs/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a
        class="button secondary"
        href="https://github.com/DevJoaoLopes/agent-interaction-kit"
        >View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
    <Ecosystem />
    <a class="scroll-cue" href="#contract-story"
      >SCROLL TO BREAK THE CONTRACT <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
    >
  </section>
  <section class="intro-band" id="contract-story">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">THE SPACE BETWEEN YOUR AGENT AND YOUR UI</span><h2>
        A small change.<br /><em>A very visible difference.</em>
      </h2><p>A renamed field can leave a perfectly connected app with nothing to show.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContractStory client:visible />
  <section class="shell quickstart" id="quickstart">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE. BUILT FOR CI.</span><h2>
        Two manifests.<br /><em>One check.</em>
      </h2><p>
        Describe what your agent provides and what your interface expects. Check the agreement
        before you ship.
      </p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Make your first contract ↗</a>
    </div><div class="terminal">
      <div class="terminal-bar">
        aik / illustrative check
      </div><pre><code>$ aik check --provider … --consumer … --strict

  ✓ getOrder
  Compatible contracts

  exit 0</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
